// The spec's own example of a sparse marker, and the first Etch-declared
// EMPTY component anywhere in the corpora.
//
// `engine-ecs-internals.md` §2 (*Table vs SparseSet*) gives the canonical tag
// shape. The spelling here is the TAG PATH, `@storage(.sparse)`: an argument
// whose declared type is an enumeration domain is written that way, as every
// sibling annotation of that shape already is, and a bare enumeration value
// would be syntactically indistinguishable from an identifier reference.
// `E0503_storage_bare_value.etch` is its refused twin.
//
// The empty body is the part that had no witness before this file. M1.B/G0
// established the zero-SIZE case has a table-side twin in production already
// (`Sleeping = extern struct {}`, `src/modules/forge/api/components.zig`), but
// no Etch source in the tree declared a fieldless component, so the spelling
// itself was unexercised. It parses because `parseComponentDecl` loops
// `while (peek() != .rbrace)` — an immediate `}` yields zero fields — and the
// type-checker carries no field-count floor.

@storage(.sparse)
component InCombat {}

@storage(.sparse)
component Stunned {}

@storage(.table)
component Health {
    current: float = 100.0
}
